<section class="section wrap">
	<h1>Race when you like</h1>
	<p class="lede">The Indoor Racing League is a handicapped Zwift league for groups of friends. No start times, no pack racing &mdash; just ride the route whenever suits you, and your time is adjusted for your ability, so anyone can win.</p>
	<div class="actions">
		<a class="button" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">Get involved</a>
		<a class="button button-outline" href="#how">How it works</a>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="how">
	<div class="wrap">
		<h2>How it works</h2>
		<ol class="steps">
			<li><strong>Ride the qualifier</strong> Ride the league's qualifier route solo and flat out, as many times as you like within the window. Your climb, flat and sprint times become your benchmark.</li>
			<li><strong>Ride each event</strong> Every two weeks there's a new route. Ride it once (or more) whenever suits you between Monday and the Sunday a fortnight later.</li>
			<li><strong>We do the maths</strong> Your time goes up on Strava automatically. We read the club leaderboard, adjust everyone's time against their benchmark, and update the standings.</li>
			<li><strong>Beat yourself, beat everyone</strong> The winner is whoever beats their own prediction by the most. Ride well and your benchmark tightens up a little for next time.</li>
		</ol>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
	<h2>The handicap</h2>
	<p>We don't ask for your FTP or weight. Your qualifier ride already tells us how you go on different terrain, compared with the rest of the group:</p>
	<div class="grid grid-3">
		<div class="card">
			<h3>Climbing</h3>
			<p>Your time on the climb segments. Mostly down to watts per kilo.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="card">
			<h3>Flat</h3>
			<p>The rest of the lap. Mostly raw power and how slippery you are.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="card">
			<h3>Sprint</h3>
			<p>Your time on the sprint segments. Short, sharp and painful.</p>
		</div>
	</div>
	<p style="margin-top:1.5rem">Each event is a <span class="badge badge-flat">flat</span>, <span class="badge badge-rolling">rolling</span> or <span class="badge badge-climbing">climbing</span> route, and the handicap leans on whichever ability matters most. Route types rotate so no one body type wins every time.</p>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
	<div class="section-head">
		<h2>Points</h2>
		<p class="section-note">The gaps are deliberately small. Turning up always matters.</p>
	</div>
	<div class="points">
		<div class="panel points-card">
			<h3>Events</h3>
			<ul class="points-list">
				<li><span class="points-value">15</span><span>for the fastest adjusted time, then one fewer per place, never less than 1</span></li>
				<li><span class="points-value">+2</span><span>every time you finish</span></li>
				<li><span class="points-value">=</span><span>tied riders share the higher place</span></li>
			</ul>
		</div>
		<div class="panel points-card">
			<h3>Qualifier</h3>
			<ul class="points-list">
				<li><span class="points-value">+2</span><span>for riding it</span></li>
				<li><span class="points-value">3·2·1</span><span>bonus for the three fastest riders on each climb and sprint</span></li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
	<div class="section-head">
		<h2>The rules</h2>
		<p class="section-note">Only initials, adjusted times and points are ever shown.</p>
	</div>
	<ol class="rules">
		<li class="panel"><strong>Ride solo</strong> No group rides, races or events. Drafting breaks the handicap.</li>
		<li class="panel"><strong>Ride the set route</strong> Flat out, within the window. Your best effort counts.</li>
		<li class="panel"><strong>Keep Strava sync on</strong> Leave Zwift's Strava sync switched on, and check your first league ride appears.</li>
		<li class="panel"><strong>Join the Strava club</strong> Your league's club, so you show up on the leaderboard.</li>
		<li class="panel"><strong>Not "Only You"</strong> Private rides don't appear on segment leaderboards.</li>
		<li class="panel"><strong>Be honest</strong> Real weight and height in Zwift, and a smart trainer or power meter if you can.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section class="cta" id="join">
	<div class="wrap cta-inner">
		<h2>Get involved</h2>
		<p>Fancy it, or want to run a league for your own group? Drop an email and we'll send you the qualifier details.</p>
		<a class="button" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">Send an email</a>
	</div>
</section>
